.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt WPA_CLI 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm wpa_cli
.Nd control a running wpa_supplicant
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl hrvB
.Op Fl p Ar dir
.Op Fl i Ar ifname
.Op Fl g Ar global_ctrl
.Op Fl G Ar seconds
.Op Fl a Ar program
.Op Fl P Ar pidfile
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Op Ar command Op Ar argument ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
sends commands to
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
through its control interface and prints the answers.
Given a
.Ar command ,
it sends that one and exits; without one, it reads commands from the
terminal with line editing and history, and prints the events
wpa_supplicant reports as they come.
.Pp
The commands used most are these:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm status
The state of the interface, the network joined, its access point and
the cipher.
.It Cm scan , scan_results
Start a scan; list the access points the last one found, with their
frequency, signal in dBm, security and name.
.It Cm signal_poll
The signal, noise and rate of the link.
.It Cm list_networks
The networks configured, with their numbers.
.It Cm add_network
Add an empty network and print its number.
.It Cm set_network Ar id variable value
Set a variable of network
.Ar id
as in
.Xr wpa_supplicant.conf 5 ;
a string value is given in double quotes.
.It Cm enable_network , select_network , remove_network Ar id
Let network
.Ar id
be chosen; choose it alone; remove it.
.It Cm save_config
Write the networks back to the configuration file, which needs
.Cm update_config=1
there.
.It Cm reconfigure
Read the configuration file again.
.It Cm disconnect , reconnect
Leave the network and stay off; join again.
.It Cm interface Op Ar ifname
List the interfaces, or send the next commands to
.Ar ifname .
.It Cm terminate
Stop wpa_supplicant.
.It Cm help
List every command.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a Ar program
Run as a daemon that runs
.Ar program
with the interface's name and
.Cm CONNECTED
or
.Cm DISCONNECTED
when wpa_supplicant joins or leaves a network.
.It Fl B
With
.Fl a ,
run in the background.
.It Fl g Ar global_ctrl
Send the commands to wpa_supplicant's global control interface.
.It Fl G Ar seconds
How often to check that wpa_supplicant still answers.
.It Fl h
Print the usage and the commands and exit.
.It Fl i Ar ifname
The interface to control; the default is the first one found in the
directory.
.It Fl p Ar dir
The control interfaces' directory;
.Pa /var/run/wpa_supplicant
by default.
.It Fl P Ar pidfile
With
.Fl a ,
write the process number to
.Ar pidfile .
.It Fl r
With
.Fl a ,
open the control interface again when wpa_supplicant restarts.
.It Fl s Ar socket
The path of the client's own socket.
.It Fl v
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Add a WPA3 network and join it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
wpa_cli -i wlan0 add_network
wpa_cli -i wlan0 set_network 0 ssid '"home"'
wpa_cli -i wlan0 set_network 0 key_mgmt SAE
wpa_cli -i wlan0 set_network 0 sae_password '"a long passphrase"'
wpa_cli -i wlan0 set_network 0 ieee80211w 2
wpa_cli -i wlan0 select_network 0
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr wpa_supplicant.conf 5 ,
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
